# Runtime data (jobs.db, logs, exports, reports) — never bake into the image.
# This pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED: it excludes `backend/data/` only. Do NOT widen
# it to `**/data` — `src/data/` holds packaged code-data (the job-signal
# vocabularies) that a service cannot run without, and shipping without it is
# issue #260's exact shape (silent degrade to "unknown", every instrument
# green).
data/

# THERE ARE DELIBERATELY NO `!` EXEMPTIONS BELOW, and that is the fix, not an
# omission.
#
# The shipped reference-data directory now lives INSIDE the package:
#
#   src/data/job_signals/  — the seniority / workplace / location term tables
#                            behind `signal_backed_lookup`, which fills
#                            'unknown' enrichment at read time, and
#                            `detect_seniority`. `_load_terms` returns {} on a
#                            missing file, so those detectors quietly answer
#                            nothing. (Moved 2026-08-12 — same bug, third time.)
#
# The `data/` rule above is root-anchored, so it never reached inside `src/`
# and there is nothing here to exempt. An exemption for a path nothing excludes
# is noise that reads like protection.
#
# What actually carries these into the image is `[tool.setuptools.package-data]`
# in backend/pyproject.toml plus `pip install .` — the WHEEL, not this file.
# `COPY . .` putting a file in the build context is not enough on its own,
# because the running code is the site-packages copy.
#
# Adding a new shipped data directory? Put it under `src/data/`, declare it in
# pyproject, and `tests/test_shipped_data.py` will check you did. It checks
# twice: once per `!` line in `.gitignore`, and once per file git actually
# TRACKS under `src/data/`. The second is the one that catches a NEW directory,
# because `.gitignore`'s `!backend/src/data/` already un-ignores the whole
# subtree — so a new directory is committable without a `!` line of its own and
# the first check never sees it. Both failure modes here are invisible at
# runtime: empty data, no exception (though both loaders now log an ERROR
# naming the path).

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache*/
# The glob matters: this repo carries .mypy_cache_core/, .mypy_cache_prof/ and
# .mypy_cache_routes/ (26.1 MB, untracked from git in 57625b6 but still on disk).
# A bare `.mypy_cache/` matches none of them, so a `railway up` from a developer
# machine shipped them into the image (backend/Dockerfile:13 is `COPY . .`).
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tests (optional — kept out to slim the image; the test suite is offline only)
tests/

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# Editor / IDE artifacts
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Local env overrides
.env
.env.*
